# Task Management Guidelines

This document outlines the process for creating and managing tasks within this project. We use a folder-based system to track the progress of features and major tasks.

## Task Directory Structure

All tasks are managed within the `TASKS/` directory in the project root. Each major feature or task should have its own dedicated folder inside `TASKS/`.

Example structure:
```
TASKS/
└── feature-name.md
```

- **`TASKS/`**: The root directory for all task-related documentation.
- **`feature-name.md`**: A markdown file named after the feature being implemented (e.g., `user-authentication`, `game-lobby-chat`).

## Task File Structure

Each file should be structured as follows:

```markdown
# Feature: [Feature Name]

A brief description of the feature and its purpose.

## Task List

- [ ] Sub-task 1
- [ ] Sub-task 2
- [x] Completed sub-task

## Implementation Plan

A detailed description of how the feature will be implemented. This can include:
- Architecture decisions
- Data flow diagrams
- Technical components needed

## Relevant Files

List of files that are created or modified for this feature.

- `path/to/file1.ts` - Description of the file's purpose.
- `path/to/file2.tsx` - Description of the file's purpose.

## Relevant Cursor Rules

If the implementation involves specific libraries, frameworks, or technologies that have corresponding Cursor Rules, they should be referenced here. This helps ensure consistency and adherence to best practices.

- [React Best Practices](mdc:.cursor/rules/lib/react.mdc)
- [Next.js Guidelines](mdc:.cursor/rules/lib/next-js.mdc)
- [Database Schema](mdc:.cursor/rules/packages/database.mdc)
```

## AI Instructions

When working on tasks, the AI should:

1.  Before starting a new feature, create a new directory in `TASKS/` and a `TASK.md` file.
2.  Break down the feature into a checklist of sub-tasks in `TASK.md`.
3.  Regularly update the `TASK.md` file to reflect progress by checking off completed tasks (`[x]`).
4.  Keep the "Relevant Files" section updated with all created or modified files.
5.  Document implementation details in the "Implementation Plan" section.
6.  Identify and link to any relevant Cursor Rules in the "Relevant Cursor Rules" section.
7.  When asked to work on a task, first consult the corresponding `TASK.md` file to understand the scope and status.
